diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The Apache HTTP service on web_server_1 is misconfigured for TLS. The HTTPS (port 443) listener is not present, so only plain HTTP (port 80) is served.

Mechanism: From host_1_1_1_1, HTTP to web1.local succeeds (HTTP/1.1 200 OK), but HTTPS connections to web1.local/10.200.0.4 are refused. Browsers that use an https bookmark or auto-upgrade to HTTPS will spin and then error out, which the user perceives as a timeout, while HTTP works fine.

Localization: On web_server_1, ss/netstat shows only 0.0.0.0:80 listening, no 443. The loaded Apache modules do not include ssl_module, and there is no SSL virtual host configured (no SSLEngine/SSLCertificate directives found). On the client, DNS for web1.
